{"name":"Spinach Dip","hex":"#b1cdac","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spinach dip","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common restaurant appetizer made from spinach and another ingredient such as mayonnaise, cream cheese, or sour cream, and usually served with tortilla chips."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinach_dip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spinach dip","blocks":[{"text":"Spinach dip is a dip that uses the vegetable spinach as a primary ingredient. Frozen spinach is often used in its preparation. Slow cookers may be used to prepare the dip, and it may be served warm, or there may be no cooking involved. Additional primary ingredients include mayonnaise, cream cheese, sour cream and cheese. Examples of accompaniments to spinach dip include bread, crackers and chips."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Spinach_%26_artichoke_dip.jpg/330px-Spinach_%26_artichoke_dip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach_dip"},{"title":"Spinach","blocks":[{"text":"Spinach is a leafy green flowering plant native to Central and Western Asia. It is of the order Caryophyllales, family Amaranthaceae, subfamily Chenopodioideae. Its leaves are a common vegetable consumed either fresh, cooked or after storage. The taste differs considerably between cooked and raw: the high oxalate content may be reduced by blanching."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg/330px-Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Spinach-dip-in-a-cob-loaf-recipe-506764-1.jpg/500px-Spinach-dip-in-a-cob-loaf-recipe-506764-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x",